{"id":"word:hebrew:H6153","type":"word","title":"עֶרֶב","subtitle":"H6153 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"dusk","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עֶרֶב (H6153) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 134 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עֶרֶב (ʻereb) means dusk First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 40."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עֶרֶב","transliteration":"ʻereb","pronunciation":"eh'-reb","strong":"H6153","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6153","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הָ/עָֽרֶב","הָ/עָ֑רֶב","בָּ/עֶ֔רֶב","עֶ֔רֶב","עֶ֥רֶב"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",51],["HRd/Ncmsa",31],["HNcmsa",25],["HTd/Ncmda",11],["HC/Rd/Ncmsa",9],["HR/Ncmsa",5],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",1],["HC/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"dusk","usage":"day, even(-ing, tide), night.","full":"H6153. ereb עֶ֫רֶב 131 noun [masculine] 1Sam 20:5 strike out הַשְּׁלִישִׁית see We Dr and others] (sun)set, evening ; — absolute ׳ע 2Kin 2:16 +, עָ֑רֶב Exod 12:18 +; construct עֶרֶב Prov 7:9 ; dual עַרְבַּיִם Exod 30:8 4 t., בָּ֑יִם - 12:16 5 t. (all P); — 1. a. evening , originally sunset, and hence perhaps ע ׳לְעֵת at the time of sunset Gen 8:11 (J), 24:11 (J; || הַשֹּׁאֲבֹת צֵאת לְעֵת ), 2Sam 11:2 ; Isa 17:14 and (of the day of ׳י ) Zech 14:7 , הָע ׳עֵת Josh 8:29 (JE) ; usually ׳ע alone = time of sunset, evening: ׳בָּע in the evening Gen 19:1 (J), 29:23 (E), Exod 12:18 (P), Deut 16:6 (+ כְּבוֺא שֶׁמֶשׁ ), 1Kin 22:35 (compare || 2Chr 18:34 where + הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ בּוֺא לְעֵת ) + 20 t. + ׳בָּע(ֿ)בָּע 13:11 (twice in verse) = every evening ; ׳לָע at evening only late: 1Chr 16:40 ; 23:30 ; 2Chr 2:3 ; Ezra 3:3 ; Psa 59:7 ; 59:15 ; 90:6 ; Eccl 11:6 ; ע ׳לִפְנוֺת at the turn of evening Gen 24:63 (J), Deut 23:12 ; ׳ע as adverb accusative Exod 16:6 (P), Psa 55:18 ; as marking duration of impurity, in phrase ׳עַדהָֿע Lev 11:24 30 t. P + 22:6 (H); of Day of Atonement ׳עַדעֿ ׳מֵע 23:32 (P). b. dual in phrase (only P) הָעַרְבַּיִם בֵּין between the two evenings , i.e. probably between sunset and dark (see Thes [various views fully given]; otherwise Di Exod 12:6 ; on form as possibly only expanded plural see Ges § 88c ), 12:6 ; 16:12 ; 29:39 , 41 ; 30:8 ; Lev 23:5 ; Num 9:3 , 5 , 11 ; 28:4 , 8 . c. other phrases are: ע ׳צִלְלֵי Jer 6:4 (distinguished from צָהֳרָ֑יִם and לָ֑יְלָה 6:5 ), (הָ)ע ׳מִנְחַה 2Kin 16:15 ; Ezra 9:4-5 , Psa 141:2 ; Dan 9:21 ; ע ׳זְאֵבֵי see I. זְאֵב ; for all combinations with בֹּקֶר morning , see ׳ב 1d, e. 2. (late poetry) = night, עָ֑רֶב Job 7:4 ; compare יוֺם בְּעֶרֶב בְּנֶשֶׁף Prov 7:9 (|| וִאֲפֵלָה לַיְלָה בְּאִישׁוֺן ).","rootNote":"from 6150 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 16 40","keyReferences":["1Chr 16 40","1Chr 23 30","1Kgs 17 6","1Kgs 22 35","1Sam 14 24","1Sam 20 5","1Sam 30 17","2Chr 2 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":134,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 16 40","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/לָ/עָ֑רֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Rd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 23 30","book":"1Chr","chapter":23,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָ/עָֽרֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/עָ֑רֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 35","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּ/עֶ֔רֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 24","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/עֶ֗רֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/עֶ֥רֶב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 30 17","book":"1Sam","chapter":30,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/עֶ֖רֶב","source"